WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.417
Henderson Island is one of the least-disturbed raised atolls in the world,

00:00:04.417 --> 00:00:06.120
but its threats arrived by sea.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:11.922
Henderson has four land birds found nowhere else: the flightless Henderson crake,

00:00:11.922 --> 00:00:16.566
the Henderson fruit dove, the Henderson lorikeet and the Henderson reed warbler.

00:00:16.566 --> 00:00:19.933
It is also the only breeding site of the Henderson petrel.

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:25.360
Pacific rats, brought by Polynesian voyagers about eight hundred years ago,

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:26.745
eat the petrels' chicks.

00:00:26.745 --> 00:00:30.842
In 2011, seventy-five tonnes of poison bait were dropped by helicopter.

00:00:30.842 --> 00:00:35.227
Genetic analysis later showed that only about sixty to eighty rats survived,

00:00:35.227 --> 00:00:38.111
but that was enough for the population to recover.

00:00:39.211 --> 00:00:40.396
Then there is plastic.

00:00:40.396 --> 00:00:42.227
Carried by the South Pacific Gyre,

00:00:42.227 --> 00:00:46.697
it has given Henderson's beaches one of the highest debris densities ever recorded:

00:00:46.697 --> 00:00:51.274
an estimated thirty-seven point seven million items, weighing about seventeen tonnes.

00:00:52.374 --> 00:00:55.264
Much of it is fishing gear, bottles and fragments,

00:00:55.264 --> 00:00:57.691
most of it washed in from other countries.

00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:01.176
Offshore, island type shapes the reefs.

00:01:01.176 --> 00:01:05.824
In 2012, divers found that coral species richness increased with island age:

00:01:05.824 --> 00:01:09.859
from twenty-four species at young Pitcairn to fifty-eight at Oeno.

00:01:09.859 --> 00:01:14.140
But that pattern rests on just four islands, so treat it with caution.
